From 4efe4a2312dab8ace6b0c40edd657dcb151b379d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kruxx <massefehler@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:44:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] charts: make menu item accessibility optional

YouTube no longer sends `selectedAccessibility`/`deselectedAccessibility` in the
country entries of the charts menu (`musicMultiSelectMenuItemRenderer`), only a
single `accessibility`. The strict model threw

  MissingFieldException: Fields [selectedAccessibility, deselectedAccessibility]
  are required for type ... ItemRendererImpl

for every FEmusic_charts response, which surfaced as "Failed to get charts" on
Kreate's home screen. Both fields are optional now; nothing reads them.

Adds the full DE response captured on 2026-09-02 as a fixture and a test that
walks the same path as InnertubeImpl.charts().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BTcqdAdg11dWBrPajTwTKr
